message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Honest Ceiling: fold-safe ensembling and a Darwin-Cage residual search on Kaggle Playground S6E9"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Angulo de Lafuente"
    given-names: "Francisco"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-01
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Agnuxo1/s6e9-honest-ceiling"
url: "https://agnuxo1.github.io/s6e9-honest-ceiling/"
keywords:
  - kaggle
  - tabular data
  - target encoding
  - out-of-fold validation
  - ensembling
  - genetic programming
  - negative results
  - power analysis
abstract: >-
  A fully fold-safe ensembling pipeline (shared outer split, nested target encoding, nested hill-climb, averaging
  over outer splits) reaches a nested out-of-fold ROC-AUC of 0.946420 on Kaggle Playground S6E9, within sampling
  error of its own oracle bound (0.94660 ± 0.00028). An evolutionary search over 47,679 feature programs, rewarded
  only by structure in the residual and confirmed on a never-seen fold, finds nothing; a power analysis with planted
  signals shows what it would have found.
